# Keep the container build context small and reproducible.
#
# `target/` is hundreds of megabytes of host-built artifacts compiled
# against the host toolchain and libc. Copying it in is slow and, worse,
# lets a stale host artifact leak into a lane whose whole purpose is to
# compile and run against a different distribution.
#
# Podman reads this file; Docker reads .dockerignore, which is a symlink
# to this one so the two lanes cannot drift apart.
target/
.git/
.atl/
